      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The journey continues!! 😅 Although the project setting is discarded, it seems like we **can** change the `velocityThreshold` at runtime via Udon. (Is that documented somewhere?)\nHowever, we *can't* do that with the `bounceThreshold` of 3d physics! 😵‍💫 I'm not sure we have access to that setting at all.\nIf we had a page for this in the VRChat documentation, I'd suggest an edit there. But we don't, so this might leave some world creators confused.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-02-28T00:27:35.852Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When using Physics 2d, we cannot change the `Velocity Threshold` in the project settings. The setting defaults to 1 inside VRChat.\nThis means that bounces to not work when a 2d phyics system is at a low velocity.\n*For example: A small 2d physics objects hits a collider. It does not bounce, because it far exeeds the minimum velocity of 1.*\nWould be lovely if we had access to this project setting. Thanks!",
